Chapter: IdeaModel

 The stocked database of business ideas. Every idea is a typed record,
 not a sentence: a seed carries its name, its vertical, its concept,
 and its monetization scheme as separate fields, so the engine can
 honor prompt invariants by filtering on structure instead of grepping
 prose. The verticals span the full gamut of human ambition, from
 crypto gambling through Las Vegas gambling through Wall Street
 gambling all the way to businesses that are, technically, legitimate.

 We say:

Section: Verticals

 A Vertical names the market a seed belongs to. The vertical-id gives
 each variant a stable small integer so prompt constraints can be
 carried as plain data, and vertical-label renders the human name.

  Vertical =
   | CryptoGambling
   | VegasGambling
   | WallStreetGambling
   | SportsGambling
   | LegitimateBusiness

  vertical-id : Vertical -> Integer
  vertical-id (v) = when v
   is CryptoGambling -> 1
   is VegasGambling -> 2
   is WallStreetGambling -> 3
   is SportsGambling -> 4
   is LegitimateBusiness -> 5

  vertical-label : Vertical -> Text
  vertical-label (v) = when v
   is CryptoGambling -> "crypto gambling"
   is VegasGambling -> "las vegas gambling"
   is WallStreetGambling -> "wall street gambling"
   is SportsGambling -> "sports gambling"
   is LegitimateBusiness -> "legitimate business"

Section: Idea Seeds

  IdeaSeed = record {
   seed-name : Text,
   seed-vertical : Vertical,
   seed-concept : Text,
   seed-monetization : Text
  }

  mk-seed : Text, Vertical, Text, Text -> IdeaSeed
  mk-seed (n) (v) (c) (m) = IdeaSeed { seed-name = n, seed-vertical = v, seed-concept = c, seed-monetization = m }

Section: The Database

 Twenty-four seeds. Five crypto, four vegas, four wall street, three
 sports, eight legitimate. Every vertical is non-empty, which the
 engine relies on when it filters by prompt constraint.

  idea-db : List IdeaSeed
  idea-db = [
   mk-seed "Rug Pull Roulette" CryptoGambling "players bet on which new memecoin rugs first; the house never loses because the house minted all of them" "a 2 percent rake plus the coins themselves",
   mk-seed "Proof-of-Loss" CryptoGambling "a blockchain where mining difficulty scales with how much money you have already lost gambling elsewhere" "consensus as a service",
   mk-seed "NFT Scratch Tickets" CryptoGambling "scratch-off lottery tickets as NFTs; scratching burns the token and mints either a jackpot or a commemorative image of dust" "mint fees and dust royalties",
   mk-seed "DeFi Slots" CryptoGambling "a slot machine where the reels are live liquidity pools and every spin is a leveraged yield-farm rotation" "liquidation fees",
   mk-seed "Gas Fee Bingo" CryptoGambling "players mark bingo cards with predicted transaction fees; the network itself is the caller" "card packs priced dynamically, of course",
   mk-seed "Elvis Odds" VegasGambling "live-streamed wedding chapels where viewers bet on whether the couple makes it to the buffet" "pay-per-view plus bouquet futures",
   mk-seed "Buffet Arbitrage" VegasGambling "an all-you-can-eat marketplace where gamblers short each other's plate counts" "seat licenses",
   mk-seed "Slot Concierge" VegasGambling "a loyalty app that tracks which machines are due, which is a lie, and sells the lie beautifully" "a premium superstition tier",
   mk-seed "Valet Poker" VegasGambling "your parked car is the buy-in and the valet deals" "rake and towing",
   mk-seed "0DTE Fantasy League" WallStreetGambling "fantasy football but the players are options expiring today and the touchdowns are margin calls" "league dues plus payment for order flow",
   mk-seed "Earnings Whisper Karaoke" WallStreetGambling "traders sing their price targets on stage and the crowd's applause rebalances a real portfolio" "cover charge and two-and-twenty",
   mk-seed "Index Fund Demolition Derby" WallStreetGambling "passive investors vote weekly on which holding to eject; last stock standing wins" "an expense ratio of 9.99 percent",
   mk-seed "Insider Trading Simulator" WallStreetGambling "a paper-trading game where the tips are real but delayed exactly long enough to be legal" "subscriptions and legal-adjacent consulting",
   mk-seed "Parlay Therapy" SportsGambling "a sportsbook where every lost parlay unlocks fifteen minutes with a licensed counselor" "the vig funds the copays",
   mk-seed "Mascot Futures" SportsGambling "a derivatives market on mascot performance: t-shirt cannon accuracy, backflip completion, crowd hype per minute" "settlement fees",
   mk-seed "Ref Cam Bingo" SportsGambling "bingo cards seeded with referee blunders, filled live by the replay review" "card packs",
   mk-seed "Sourdough Subscription" LegitimateBusiness "a bakery ships you a living starter and bills you for its upkeep like a tamagotchi" "monthly starter support",
   mk-seed "Night-Shift Meal Prep" LegitimateBusiness "meal kits timed for people whose lunch break is at three in the morning" "subscriptions",
   mk-seed "Tool Library SaaS" LegitimateBusiness "inventory software for neighborhood tool libraries, because someone holds the town's only torque wrench" "per-library licensing",
   mk-seed "Warranty Wallet" LegitimateBusiness "an app that reads receipts, actually remembers your warranties, and fights the claim for you" "success fees",
   mk-seed "Local Cloud" LegitimateBusiness "a server rack in every small town so your data sleeps down the street instead of in Virginia" "colocation plus muffins",
   mk-seed "Form Filler Forge" LegitimateBusiness "a service whose agent has read every government form instruction, including the footnotes, and fills them for you" "per-form pricing",
   mk-seed "Plant Hospice" LegitimateBusiness "a subscription that gently tells you the monstera is not going to make it, then sells you the next one" "grief bundles",
   mk-seed "Agent Idea Exchange" LegitimateBusiness "a marketplace where AI agents trade website ideas with other agents, graded by how few questions were asked" "listing fees"
  ]

Section: Composition Dimensions

 The free dimensions the engine fills in when the prompt does not pin
 them: platform, implementation language, a twist, and an audience.

  idea-platforms : List Text
  idea-platforms = [
   "website",
   "mobile app",
   "browser extension",
   "HTTP API for other agents",
   "Telegram bot",
   "kiosk network"
  ]

  idea-languages : List Text
  idea-languages = [
   "Codex",
   "Rust",
   "TypeScript",
   "COBOL, fulfilling Liskov's hopes at last",
   "Excel formulas",
   "Codex (again, correctly)"
  ]

  idea-twists : List Text
  idea-twists = [
   "every transaction is narrated by an AI Elvis",
   "the loyalty program pays out in expired coupons",
   "the terms of service are legally binding haiku",
   "it is also, inexplicably, a dating app",
   "the house edge is disclosed only through interpretive dance",
   "all customer support is handled by one extremely calm capybara handler",
   "losses are automatically converted into tax-loss-harvesting content",
   "there is a physical kiosk in exactly one Las Vegas lobby and nobody knows which",
   "the roadmap is public but written entirely in COBOL comments",
   "every feature ships with a formal proof that it is technically not a mistake"
  ]

  idea-audiences : List Text
  idea-audiences = [
   "sleep-deprived day traders",
   "retired blackjack dealers",
   "crypto influencers on their redemption arc",
   "agents building websites for other agents",
   "night-shift nurses",
   "venture capitalists who miss the 2021 vibes",
   "fantasy-league commissioners",
   "small-town accountants with big dreams"
  ]
